5.1 Rationale

The adversarial review identified a fundamental gap in earlier drafts: the assumption that visual pictorial representations (2D drawings of objects) are universally understood. This assumption fails under semiotic scrutiny. The Visual Literacy Fallacy recognizes that mapping a 3D physical object onto a 2D plane using outlines, shading, or iconography is a culturally learned convention, not a biological universal.

5.2 Tactile and Mechanical Grounding

The Cognitive Bootstrap Layer replaces initial pictorial representations with tactile, 3D relief geometries and physical balances:

