8.1 Architectural Foundations

The Universal Information Representation (UIR) serves as the formal bridge between abstract symbolic logic and universal constants (C1–C3) and empirical physical domain knowledge (C5–C11). To eliminate semantic drift and language dependence, the UIR is formalized as an Empirically Anchored Operational Formal System. A term in UIR does not derive meaning from a natural language dictionary; rather, its denotational semantics are defined strictly by a tuple of universal physical constants ($\mathcal{C}_{C3}$), geometric invariants, and reproducible physical state-transition protocols (EVP).

8.2 Mathematical Universe Definition

Let $\mathcal{U}_{UIR} = \langle \mathcal{C}_{C3}, \mathcal{V}, \mathcal{T}, \mathcal{E}, \llbracket \cdot \rrbracket \rangle$ be the UIR signature, where:

· $\mathcal{C}_{C3} = \{\Delta \nu_{\text{Cs}}, c, h, e, k_B, N_A\}$ is the basis set of C3-anchored physical constants.
