8.4 Type System and Dimensional Integrity

To prevent illogical statements, the UIR type checker enforces strict dimensional conservation rules over the dimension vector $\mathbf{d} \in \mathbb{Z}^6$:

\mathbf{d} = \begin{bmatrix} \text{TIME} & \text{LENGTH} & \text{MASS} & \text{CHARGE} & \text{TEMP} & \text{AMOUNT} \end{bmatrix}^T

Typability Rules:

Dimensional Multiplication/Division:

\frac{\Gamma \vdash e_1 : \mathbf{d}_1 \quad \Gamma \vdash e_2 : \mathbf{d}_2}{\Gamma \vdash e_1 \cdot e_2 : \mathbf{d}_1 + \mathbf{d}_2} \quad \text{and} \quad \frac{\Gamma \vdash e_1 : \mathbf{d}_1 \quad \Gamma \vdash e_2 : \mathbf{d}_2}{\Gamma \vdash e_1 / e_2 : \mathbf{d}_1 - \mathbf{d}_2}

Additive Homogeneity Constraint:

\frac{\Gamma \vdash e_1 : \mathbf{d}_1 \quad \Gamma \vdash e_2 : \mathbf{d}_2 \quad \mathbf{d}_1 = \mathbf{d}_2}{\Gamma \vdash e_1 + e_2 : \mathbf{d}_1}

If $\mathbf{d}_1 \neq \mathbf{d}_2$, the expression $e_1 + e_2$ is ill-typed and fails compilation.

